# Environment variables.
# Deny everything, then re-admit only the templates. The previous rules listed
# `.env`, `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`, which left `.env.production` — the
# file holding the real OPENAI_API_KEY and POSTGRES_PASSWORD — perfectly
# committable. An allowlist fails safe: a new .env.<something> is ignored by
# default instead of needing someone to remember to add a rule.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

